    <location value="28"/>
    ROOF ASSEMBLIES AND ROOFTOP STRUCTURES
  </page_header>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>6.7.5.4</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="61"/>
    <location value="37"/>
    <location value="454"/>
    <location value="52"/>
    Material standards. Metal roof shingle roof coverings shall comply with Table 6.7.4.3.
    <ldiv>
      <marker>6.7.5.5</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="61"/>
    <location value="54"/>
    <location value="454"/>
    <location value="69"/>
<![CDATA[Attachment. Metal roof shingles shall be secured to the roof in accordance with the approved manufacturer's installation instructions.]]>    
    <ldiv>
      <marker>6.7.5.6</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="61"/>
    <location value="71"/>
    <location value="454"/>
    <location value="119"/>
    Flashing. Roof valley flashing shall  be  of  corrosion-resistant  metal  of  the  same material as the roof covering or shall comply with the standards in Table 6.7.4.3. The valley flashing shall extend at least 200 mm from the centerline each way and shall have a splash diverter rib not less than 19 mm high at the flow line formed as part of the flashing. Sections of flashing shall have an end lap of not less than 100 mm.
  </list>
  <heading level="2">
    <location value="200"/>
    <location value="125"/>
    <location value="315"/>
    <location value="138"/>
    TABLE 6.7.4.3 METAL ROOF COVERINGS
  </heading>
  <table>
    <location value="91"/>
    <location value="142"/>
    <location value="421"/>
    <location value="258"/>
    <ched/>
    ROOF COVERING TYPE
    <ched/>
