  </table>
  <list class="ordered">
    <ldiv>
      <marker>6.7.6</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="61"/>
    <location value="268"/>
    <location value="454"/>
    <location value="283"/>
    Mineral-surfaced roll roofing. The installation of mineral-surfaced roll roofing shall comply with this section.
    <ldiv>
      <marker>6.7.6.1</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="61"/>
    <location value="285"/>
    <location value="454"/>
    <location value="299"/>
    Deck  requirements. Mineral-surfaced  roll  roofing  shall  be  fastened  to  solidly sheathed roofs.
    <ldiv>
      <marker>6.7.6.2</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="61"/>
    <location value="301"/>
    <location value="454"/>
    <location value="316"/>
    Deck  slope. Mineral-surfaced  roll  roofing  shall  not  be  applied  on  roof  slopes below one unit vertical in 12 units horizontal (8 percent slope).
    <ldiv>
      <marker>6.7.6.3</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="61"/>
    <location value="318"/>
    <location value="446"/>
    <location value="333"/>
    Underlayment. Underlayment shall conform to ASTM D 226, Type I. Exception: Detached accessory structures that contain no conditioned floor area.
    <ldiv>
      <marker>6.7.6.4</marker>
    </ldiv>
    <location value="61"/>
    <location value="335"/>
    <location value="454"/>
    <location value="350"/>
    Material standards. Mineral-surfaced roll roofing shall conform to ASTM D 224, ASTM D 249, ASTM D 371 or ASTM D 3909.
